# Superword packs (src/wasm.ts `slpPlan`, `#emitPack`): groups of four isomorphic lane-wise u32
# operations, seeded by the four-element groups of u32 array literals and grown through their
# operands, each done as one i32x4 operation. Frame 0 only (no host), with the simd option.
# This part was written in the A0S form of tools/a0s.ts and expanded by it.
#
# The plan (`wyplan`) is computed per variant into a scratch table S (u32x128x512), then the
# part emission needs is copied into M (`wyput`). Words of S: per node k of the function
# (2816 each) 0 + k packed (4 (c + 1) + lane of the first pack in post order holding k, 0
# none), 2816 + k scalar, 5632 + k leaf reads, 8448 + k holder (as packed), 11264 + k read as a
# scalar by a node that is not pack-only (or by the ret), 14080 + k inline; 16896 + 16 c pack c
# (creation order): 0-3 lanes, 4 op, 5 swap bits, 6 7 kid kinds (0 pack, 1 same, 2 lanes), 8 9
# kid packs, 10 ready + 1, 11 demand bits, 12 search state, 14 post order index; 18944 + j the
# packs in post order (src/wasm.ts `packs`), 19072 + r the packs by (ready, post order), 19200 +
# j the emission order, 19328.. registers, 19392.. the search stack, 32768 + s operand slot s
# is a group of an array literal stored from its pack (it reads no lane).
# Words of M: 19120 the pack count (0: no packs), 19124 + k/32 bit k%32 node k is not emitted
# (pack-only or inline), 19212 + k/32 inline, 19300 + k/32 pack-only (holder), 19392 + 4i
# pack i (post order): lane0 | lane1 << 16, lane2 | lane3 << 16, op | swap << 4 | kid kinds
# << 8, 10 | kid packs << 12, 20, ready + 1 | demand << 12 | v128 local << 16; 19904 + j the
# emission order (post order indices); 20032 the kids kept in a v128 local (src/wasm.ts `#kept`),
# 20033 + e kept kid e: pack (post order) | side << 8 | v128 local << 16; 20296 + 8 s form slot s
# (see `wyfm`), 20320 20321 20322 registers of `wyfk`.
fn wyfnd u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
q0 mul p1 16
b add 16896 q0
q1 shr b 7
q2 and b 127
q3 get p2 q1
